> ## Quest: **The Trail of the Bone-Merchant**
> 
> **Hook:** A frightened mountain trader says the Bone-Merchant has been buying monster remains and stealing old guardian-statues. His newest creation, the **Ridgebreaker**, is nearly finished—and it may be headed toward Redclaw territory.
> 
> Ekemon has rough directions: “Follow the three stone teeth, find the singing bridge, then ask for Old Nessa.”
> 
> ### 1. The Three Stone Teeth
> Three jagged peaks overlook a narrow pass. A rockslide has trapped a pair of travelers, including **Toma**, a young goblin scavenger who once sold bones to the Merchant.
> 
> - **Challenge:** Move rocks (Athletics DC 11), find a safe route (Survival DC 11), or fight 2–3 **Bone-Crows**—little bird skeleton constructs.
> - **Clue:** Toma reveals that the Merchant’s workers mark safe paths with a symbol: a **circle made of three bones**.
> - **Choice:** Help Toma recover his lost climbing pack; he becomes a friendly guide for one later scene.
> 
> ### 2. The Singing Bridge
> A wind-harp bridge crosses a deep ravine. It hums different notes when something magical approaches.
> 
> - **Fight:** The bridge is guarded by a **Stonehorn Ram** construct (use wolf/bear stats, but resistance to nonmagical slashing if desired).
> - **Twist:** The ram is protecting a trapped mountain goat, not attacking randomly. Ekemon can defeat it, distract it, or free the goat and calm it.
> - **Clue:** Etched underneath the bridge: “**Nessa knows the price of a heart.**”
> 
> ### 3. Old Nessa’s Refuge
> Old Nessa is a retired dwarf golem-maker living in a warm cave full of kettles, gears, and harmless tiny clay servants.
> 
> She worked with the Bone-Merchant long ago, when he was called **Master Vell**. He once made protective guardians, but became obsessed with building a “perfect Titan-beast.”
> 
> - Nessa explains his weakness: his creations obey a **bone-whistle** tuned to his workshop’s forge-fire.
> - She gives Ekemon a choice:
>   - **Whistle-cracker:** Can disrupt one construct for a round.
>   - **Forge-key:** Opens a secret workshop entrance.
>   - **Guardian charm:** Lets Ekemon persuade one creation that it is not a monster.
> 
> ### 4. The Shardbone Mine
> Following old mining rails leads to Vell’s hidden workshop. Along the way, Ekemon finds people who have worked for him: frightened kobold miners and a stern ogre courier.
> 
> - **Choice:** Free/persuade them, sneak past, or fight.
> - If helped, they reveal the workshop’s secret entrance and warn that the Ridgebreaker is unfinished.
> 
> ### 5. The Bone-Merchant’s Forge
> Master Vell stands in a huge forge-cave, assembling the **Ridgebreaker**: a towering monster-bone golem with a glowing heart-cage.
> 
> - **Boss battle:** Vell plus 1–2 smaller constructs; the Ridgebreaker wakes halfway through.
> - Ekemon can:
>   - Smash the forge controls.
>   - Use Nessa’s item to confuse or free the Ridgebreaker.
>   - Fight Vell directly.
>   - Convince Vell that making living creatures into tools is cowardly—not Titan-worthy.
> 
> **Victory rewards:** a Titan-forged upgrade for Ekemon’s weapon, rescued allies for Titan Camp, and a mysterious **Heartbone Fragment** that may respond to his Titan Seed.
